.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2019\/08\/20190810_182912\/2931496381.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">In front of the <i>Halles<\/i> (i.e. covered market) fly both the French and the American flags. The American flag is pictured to thank the American soldiers that landed on the coasts of Normandie to help free France from German occupation.<\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/08\/20190810_200735.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"While Etretat might be famous for its &lt;i&gt;falaises&lt;\/i&gt;, all the cities along the Normandie coast have gorgeous falaise, including Yport pictured here.\" data-attachment-id=\"4660\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"While Etretat might be famous for its &lt;i&gt;falaises&lt;\/i&gt;, all the cities along the Normandie coast have gorgeous falaise, including Yport pictured here.\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2019\/08\/20190810_200735\/341371833.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">While Etretat might be famous for its <i>falaises<\/i>, all the cities along the Normandie coast have gorgeous falaise, including Yport pictured here.<\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/08\/20190810_180525.jpg\" data-attachment-id=\"4655\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2019\/08\/20190810_180525\/1804867988.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/08\/20190810_203929.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"View from the top of the cliffs at Yport. (The city is adamant about the fact that these cliffs could crumble at any moment and advises to not approach the edge.)\" data-attachment-id=\"4661\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"View from the top of the cliffs at Yport. (The city is adamant about the fact that these cliffs could crumble at any moment and advises to not approach the edge.)\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2019\/08\/20190810_203929\/2310802522.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">View from the top of the cliffs at Yport. (The city is adamant about the fact that these cliffs could crumble at any moment and advises to not approach the edge.)<\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/08\/20190810_210700.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"However, approaching the edge does give the benefit of a nice sunset to end a lively day.\" data-attachment-id=\"4662\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"However, approaching the edge does give the benefit of a nice sunset to end a lively day.\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2019\/08\/20190810_210700\/1252521421.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">However, approaching the edge does give the benefit of a nice sunset to end a lively day.<\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><\/div>\r\n\n<\/div>\n<div class=\"su-tabs-pane su-u-clearfix su-u-trim\" data-title=\"B\u00e9n\u00e9dictine Palace\">\n<style type=\"text\/css\">\r\n\t#foogallery-gallery-4669 .fg-image {\r\n        width: 150px;\r\n    }\r\n<\/style>\r\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"foogallery foogallery-container foogallery-default foogallery-lightbox-foobox fg-gutter-10 fg-center fg-default fg-light fg-border-thin fg-shadow-outline fg-loading-default fg-loaded-fade-in fg-caption-hover fg-hover-fade fg-hover-zoom fg-ready\" id=\"foogallery-gallery-4669\" data-foogallery=\"{&quot;item&quot;:{&quot;showCaptionTitle&quot;:true,&quot;showCaptionDescription&quot;:true},&quot;lazy&quot;:true}\" >\r\n\t<div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/08\/20190811_115014.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"The B\u00e9n\u00e9dictine Palace as we know it today was completed in 1900. The architect Camille Albert was commissioned to build the palace by Alexandre Le Grand, the owner of a mysterious French liqueur named B\u00e9n\u00e9dictine. The palace was to serve as a museum and factory for the special beverage.\" data-attachment-id=\"4663\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"The B\u00e9n\u00e9dictine Palace as we know it today was completed in 1900. The architect Camille Albert was commissioned to build the palace by Alexandre Le Grand, the owner of a mysterious French liqueur named B\u00e9n\u00e9dictine. The palace was to serve as a museum and factory for the special beverage.\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2019\/08\/20190811_115014\/608672598.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">The B\u00e9n\u00e9dictine Palace as we know it today was completed in 1900. The architect Camille Albert was commissioned to build the palace by Alexandre Le Grand, the owner of a mysterious French liqueur named B\u00e9n\u00e9dictine. The palace was to serve as a museum and factory for the special beverage.<\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/08\/20190811_115925.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"In 1510, the monk Dom Bernardo Vincelli was sent to the F\u00e9camp Abbey (in France) from Italy in 1509. He was an alchemist in search of the ultimate cure-all. He came over from Italy with various herbs and spices from around the world, some of which are used in the B\u00e9n\u00e9dictine recipe. The alcohol was produced for three centuries until the French Revolution, when the monks had to flee and go into hiding. One of the monks from that period, Dom Louis-Ambroise Blandin, gave the recipe to Prosper Coillard, who was the grand-father of Alexandre Le Grand, who later discovered the recipe. The seal of the Abbey can be seen in a smaller glass window above. It was later chosen by Alexandre Le Grand as the symbol of the alcohol.\" data-attachment-id=\"4665\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"In 1510, the monk Dom Bernardo Vincelli was sent to the F\u00e9camp Abbey (in France) from Italy in 1509. He was an alchemist in search of the ultimate cure-all. He came over from Italy with various herbs and spices from around the world, some of which are used in the B\u00e9n\u00e9dictine recipe. The alcohol was produced for three centuries until the French Revolution, when the monks had to flee and go into hiding. One of the monks from that period, Dom Louis-Ambroise Blandin, gave the recipe to Prosper Coillard, who was the grand-father of Alexandre Le Grand, who later discovered the recipe. The seal of the Abbey can be seen in a smaller glass window above. It was later chosen by Alexandre Le Grand as the symbol of the alcohol.\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2019\/08\/20190811_115925\/710749000.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">In 1510, the monk Dom Bernardo Vincelli was sent to the F\u00e9camp Abbey (in France) from Italy in 1509. He was an alchemist in search of the ultimate cure-all. He came over from Italy with various herbs and spices from around the world, some of which are used in the B\u00e9n\u00e9dictine recipe. The alcohol was produced for three centuries until the French Revolution, when the monks had to flee and go into hiding. One of the monks from that period, Dom Louis-Ambroise Blandin, gave the recipe to Prosper Coillard, who was the grand-father of Alexandre Le Grand, who later discovered the recipe. The seal of the Abbey can be seen in a smaller glass window above. It was later chosen by Alexandre Le Grand as the symbol of the alcohol.<\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/08\/20190811_115422.jpg\" data-caption-desc=\"The Palace displays an interesting mix of gothic and renaissance styles. Facing the stained-glass window of Dom Bernardo Vincelli the alchemist is a statue of Dom Bernardo Vincelli the pious.\" data-attachment-id=\"4664\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2019\/08\/20190811_115422\/2407340476.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-desc\">The Palace displays an interesting mix of gothic and renaissance styles. Facing the stained-glass window of Dom Bernardo Vincelli the alchemist is a statue of Dom Bernardo Vincelli the pious.<\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/08\/20190811_120851.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"It was carpenters from the nearby port of F\u00e9camp who built the roof of this room. This becomes very obvious if you try to picture the roof upside down. It&#039;s a boat! That\u2019s what the carpenters were skilled at doing and that\u2019s what they did. Currently, this room houses some of the religious objects of the Abbey that was abandoned.\" data-attachment-id=\"4666\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"It was carpenters from the nearby port of F\u00e9camp who built the roof of this room. This becomes very obvious if you try to picture the roof upside down. It&#039;s a boat! That\u2019s what the carpenters were skilled at doing and that\u2019s what they did. Currently, this room houses some of the religious objects of the Abbey that was abandoned.\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2019\/08\/20190811_120851\/3444673808.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20